Why Is Wi-Fi HaLow Becoming Important for IoT Connectivity?

Wi-Fi HaLow is based on the IEEE 802.11ah wireless networking standard and operates in sub-GHz frequency bands. Unlike conventional Wi-Fi technologies operating primarily at 2.4GHz and 5GHz, Wi-Fi HaLow is designed to provide extended communication range and improved signal penetration.

Its characteristics make the technology relevant to connected devices that operate across larger buildings, industrial facilities and outdoor environments.

A Wi-Fi HaLow SoC integrates wireless communication functionality with supporting processing and interface capabilities. This allows manufacturers to develop compact connectivity solutions for IoT devices without requiring multiple discrete communication components.

Long-Range IoT Applications Are Driving Market Growth

One of the major factors influencing the Wi-Fi HaLow SoC Market is the growing deployment of connected devices across industrial and commercial environments.

Traditional short-range wireless solutions may require several access points or network infrastructure components when devices are distributed across large areas.

Wi-Fi HaLow can support communication over longer distances, making it relevant to applications involving warehouses, agricultural fields, industrial facilities and connected infrastructure.

Its ability to support numerous devices within a wireless network also makes it suitable for IoT deployments requiring scalable connectivity.

